+4.1 Put $E_0:=E$. By finitely iterating the square-root axiom, choose entourages $E_1,\ldots,E_n$ such that $E_{k+1}\circ E_{k+1}\subseteq E_k$ for $0\le k<n$, and put $D:=E_n\cap E_n^{-1}$. [A1, choose]
+
+5.1 The entourage $D$ is symmetric and $D\subseteq E_n$. Induction on $k$ gives $D^{\circ 2^k}\subseteq E_{n-k}$ for $0\le k\le n$, hence $D^{\circ 2^n}\subseteq E$. Since every entourage contains the diagonal and $n\le 2^n$, one may insert diagonal factors to obtain $D^{\circ n}\subseteq D^{\circ 2^n}\subseteq E$. [step 4.1, A1, algebra]
+
+6.1 Therefore symmetric entourages form a base and admit the asserted finite-composite control. [step 3.1, step 5.1] ∎
